le guidance. Internal sidebar/authored links use native GET without document reload, with one current-page marker and deliberate heading focus; hydration preserves initial focus.\\\",\\ndocs/verification/critical-journeys.json:192:        \\\"After printed local addresses, served-page readiness retries only 502/503 for at most fifteen seconds; actual browser navigation still requires 200 and its expected heading.\\\",\\ndocs/verification/critical-journeys.json:194:        \\\"All accepted pages serve their exact processed body at the original address with checked Markdown preference and explicit .md links; GET/HEAD headers, Vary preservation, browser links and safe invalid/missing/unavailable replies hold without personal report downloads.\\\",\\ndocs/verification/critical-journeys.json:195:        \\\"All accepted documentation pages have deterministic bounded 1200 by 630 PNG share assets, actual static GET/HEAD media/cache and matching HTML metadata/decoded TechArticle; Chromium decodes every served image and build-only renderer/WebAssembly stay out of Worker/browser outputs.\\\",\\ndocs/verification/critical-journeys.json:196:        \\\"Modern MCP lists six canonical tools; its actual network client gets the same retained report and accepted Markdown page as HTTP. Alternating HTTP/MCP calculations exhaust one local allowance, with safe manual-retry failure and no submitted figures in captured logs.\\\"\\ndocs/verification/critical-journeys.json:205:      \\\"oracle\\\": \\\"Actual native built artifacts run in workerd; real Chromium independently confirms the exact RPC endpoint, no initial/replayed call, no trace/cookie headers and the retained answer. The API artifact contains the engine marker while browser artifacts must not. The generated native settings identity, short request marker and source-built internal defect require actual responses and positive fixed reporting; removing the owning failure boundary makes marker reflection fail the saved test. Unknown native function-address requests must return empty 404 and must omit the short request marker from actual native logs; removing exact-address admission restores that log leak. Actual built API global/procedure/fatal replies use fixed safe values; expected/version errors retain checked identity. A source-built damaged valid-JSON reply must restore a checked error through the genuine Website binding, with real Chromium editing and no replay. Positive fixed host logs omit the marker and pay values. Removal of each native encoder or the owned reply decoder must fail the saved test, followed by exact restoration and fresh dependency/artifact builds. Controlled API roots retain the real calculation/encoding and delay headers or the remaining body for twelve seconds. Actual generated clients must hit the ten-second deadline; Chromium must observe request abort after deadline, editing and actual Back route departure. Removing deadline or edit interruption fails the saved test; exact restoration and fresh builds pass. Pay-value checks inspect emitted log messages; private text checks inspect the whole record. Actual native mock-plan properties and saved real CLI state must contain the disabled collection policy; removing the API graph property fails the saved state Schema after runtime checks. These are declared-state checks, not cloud upload or exported-row proof. An actual successful browser answer survives edits, controlled unavailable retry and invalid form without being presented as current. Reverting figures makes no request and still needs one explicit real RPC to clear the stale message. Actual Worker-generated successful submission HTML hydrates without replay and retains its answer through editing and failed retry. The additional pages must independently return both known results via real API artifacts; no calculation fi…3090 tokens truncated…ing-and-quality.md:1454:navigation assertions. The focused browser fixture mounts the actual search\\ndocs/architecture/te