`allow_eval_during_startup` flag is set, Workers can use `eval()` and `new Function(text)` during the startup phase of a Worker script. ... ### Enable `Request.signal`","title":"Compatibility flags · Cloudflare Workers docs","url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/compatibility-flags/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.cloudflare.com","ref_id":"turn49search4","snippet":"This base class provides a set of optional methods, frequently referred to as handler methods, which can respond to events, for example a `webSocketMessage` when","title":"Durable Object Base Class · Cloudflare Durable Objects docs","url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/api/base/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.cloudflare.com","ref_id":"turn49search5","snippet":"Projects requiring HTTP request/response flows or legacy projects can continue to invoke the `fetch()` handler on the Durable Object class. ... If your project is","title":"Invoke methods · Cloudflare Durable Objects docs","url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/best-practices/create-durable-object-stubs-and-send-requests/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"9a798b9b.previews.developers.cloudflare.com","ref_id":"turn49search6","snippet":"* The Durable Object streams an incrementing number every second, until it receives `AbortSignal`. ... async fetch(request) { ... async function* dataSource(signal: AbortSignal) { ...","title":"Use ReadableStream with Durable Object and Workers · Cloudflare Durable Objects docs","url":"https://9a798b9b.previews.developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/examples/readable-stream/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.cloudflare.com","ref_id":"turn49search7","snippet":"Assuming a Durable Object does not run, the first incoming request or event (like an alarm) will execute the `constructor()` of the Durable Object class,","title":"Lifecycle of a Durable Object · Cloudflare Durable Objects docs","url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/concepts/durable-object-lifecycle/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs-durable-objects-instance-replaced-errors.previews.developers.cloudflare.com","ref_id":"turn49search8","snippet":"On the client side, `fetch()` called on a service binding or Durable Object stub works like the standard global `fetch()`. ... Again, this behavior is","title":"Workers RPC — Reserved Methods · Cloudflare Workers docs","url":"https://docs-durable-objects-instance-replaced-errors.previews.developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/rpc/reserved-methods/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.cloudflare.com","ref_id":"turn49search9","snippet":"JavaScript Errors with the property `.retryable` set to True are suggested to be retried if requests to the Durable Object are idempotent, or can be","title":"Error handling · Cloudflare Durable Objects docs","url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/best-practices/error-handling/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.cloudflare.com","ref_id":"turn49search10","snippet":"There are normal operations like code deployments that trigger Durable Objects to restart and lose their in-memory state. ... Additionally, SQLite-backed Durable Objects allow you","title":"Access Durable Objects Storage · Cloudflare Durable Objects docs","url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/best-practices/access-durable-objects-storage/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"d1-custom-bindings-docs.previews.developers.cloudflare.com","ref_id":"turn49search11","snippet":"This base class provides a set of optional methods, frequently referred to as handler methods, which can respond to events, for example a `webSocketMessage` when","title":"Durable Object Base Class · Cloudflare Durable Objects docs","url":"https://d1-custom-bindings-docs.previews.developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/api/base/"}]},"started_at_ms":1791338152811,"completed_at_ms":1791338155206}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T01:55:55.333Z","ordinal":58679,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6744f9cf-58e2-4d77-bbfb-cb670d4a949b","process_id":"66790","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","head -n 65 node_modules/effect/src/ai/McpServer.ts && rg --files node_modules/effect/src | rg 'mcpRuntime|McpRuntime|mcp.*[Rr]untime|mcp.*[Pp]rotocol'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"head -n 65 node_modules/effect/src/ai/McpServer.ts","name":"McpServer.ts","path":"node_modules/effect/src/ai/McpServer.ts"},{"type":"list_files","cmd":"rg --files node_modules/effect/src","path":"effect"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg 'mcpRuntime|McpRuntime|mcp.*[Rr]untime|mcp.*[Pp]rotocol'","query":"mcpRuntime|McpRuntime|mcp.*[Rr]untime|mcp.*[Pp]rotocol","path":null}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"/**\n * Builds Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers with Effect.\n *\n * The `McpServer` service stores the tools, resources, resource templates,\n * prompts, completions, and outgoing notifications exposed by a server. This\n * module also includes the server runner, custom protocol,\n * stdio, and HTTP layers, registration helpers, and APIs that let handlers ask\n * the connected client for structured input or read its advertised\n * capabilities.\n *\n * @stability unstable\n * @since 4.0.0\n */\nimport * as Arr from \"../Array.ts\"\nimport * as Cause from \"../Cause.ts\"\nimport * as Context from \"../Context.ts\"\nimport * as Data from \"../Data.ts\"\nimport * as Deferred from \"../Deferred.ts\"\nimport * as Effect from \"../Effect.ts\"\nimport * as ErrorReporter from \"../ErrorReporter.ts\"\nimport * as Exit from \"../Exit.ts\"\nimport * as Fiber from \"../Fiber.ts\"\nimport * as FindMyWay from \"../http/FindMyWay.ts\"\nimport * as Headers from \"../http/Hea