{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T02:25:45.215Z","ordinal":59405,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-beafb0cd-5a82-4ff7-a527-0fc768de4c8a","process_id":"39368","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","tail -5 /private/tmp/dev77-browser-saved-lifetime-native-a-native-all.log; sed -n '180,205p' /private/tmp/dev77-browser-frozen-release-a-release-graph.log"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"tail -5 /private/tmp/dev77-browser-saved-lifetime-native-a-native-all.log; sed -n '180,205p' /private/tmp/dev77-browser-frozen-release-a-release-graph.log"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"\n RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/apps/web\n\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"\n RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/apps/web\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7167},"formatted_output":"\n RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/apps/web\n\n"},"started_at_ms":1791339945215,"completed_at_ms":1791339945215}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T02:25:45.269Z","ordinal":59406,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1142e-5d35-7643-9b56-49d0d5fa517b","call_id":"call_mJdTBfadhvFfIgT74UxQiATB","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__linear_get_workspace\",\"description\":\"Plan and build products\\n\\nRetrieve the connected Linear workspace. This tool is part of plugin `Linear`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linear_get_workspace(args: { [key: string]: unknown; }): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__linear_list_comments\",\"description\":\"Plan and build products\\n\\nList comments on a Linear issue, project, initiative, document, project milestone, or project/initiative status update. Provide exactly one of `issueId`, `projectId`, `initiativeId`, `documentId`, `milestoneId`, or `statusUpdateId`. For issues, projects, and initiatives this returns both top-level discussion threads and inline description comments. Inline (anchored) comments carry a non-null `quotedText` set to the snippet of description text they reference. Returned comments include `author` and nullable `onBehalfOf`; when set, `onBehalfOf` identifies the user the agent author acted for. This tool is part of plugin `Linear`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linear_list_comments(args: {\\n  // Next page cursor\\n  cursor?: string;\\n  // Document ID or slug (provide exactly one parent)\\n  documentId?: string;\\n  // Initiative name, ID, identifier (e.g., INIT-123), or slug (provide exactly one parent)\\n  initiativeId?: string;\\n  // Issue ID or identifier (e.g., LIN-123) (provide exactly one parent)\\n  issueId?: string;\\n  // Max results (default 50, max 250)\\n  limit?: number;\\n  // Milestone UUID (provide exactly one parent). Resolve milestone names via `list_milestones` first.\\n  milestoneId?: string;\\n  // Sort: createdAt | updatedAt\\n  orderBy?: \\\"createdAt\\\" | \\\"updatedAt\\\";\\n  // Project name, ID, identifier (e.g., PROJ-123), or slug (provide exactly one parent)\\n  projectId?: string;\\n  // Status update UUID (provide exactly one parent). Resolve status updates via `get_status_updates` first.\\n  statusUpdateId?: string;\\n  // Type of status update named by `statusUpdateId`, as returned by `get_status_updates`. Only valid together with `statusUpdateId`; omit to check both project and initiative status updates.\\n  statusUpdateType?: \\\"project\\\" | \\\"initiative\\\";\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__linear_save_comment\",\"description\":\"Plan and build products\\n\\nCreate or update a comment on a Linear issue, project, initiative, document, project milestone, or project/initiative status update. If `id` is provided, updates the existing comment; otherwise creates a new one. To start a new thread, pass `body` and exactly one of `issueId`, `projectId`, `initiativeId`, `documentId`, `milestoneId`, or `statusUpdateId` — comments on issues/projects/initiatives become top-level discussion threads; comments on documents/milestones become description comments. A status update holds a single thread, so a comment on an update that already has one is added to it as a reply. To reply to an existing thread, pass `parentId` and `body`; the reply inherits the parent's thread type, so no entity reference is needed. Parent reference fields are ignored when `id` or `parentId` is provided (`statusUpdateType` is rejected instead). This tool is part of plugin `Linear`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linear_save_comment(args: {\\n  // Content as Markdown. Do not escape the string — use literal newlines and special characters, not escape sequences. To mention a user, use @displayName (e.g., @johndoe)\\n  body: string;\\n  // Document ID or slug (provide exactly one parent)\\n  documentId?: string;\\n  // Comment ID. If provided, updates the existing comment\\n  id?: string;\\n  // Initiative name, ID, identifier (e.g., INIT-123), or slug (provide exactly one parent)\\n  initiativeId?: string;\\n  // Issue ID or identifier (e.g., LIN-123) (provide exactly one parent)\\n  issueId?: string;\\n  // Milestone UUID (provide exactly one parent). Resolve milestone names via `list_milestones` first.\\n  milestoneId?: string;\\n  // Parent comment ID (for replies, only when creating)\\n  parentId?: string;\\n  // Project name, ID, identifier (e.g., PROJ-123), or slug (provide exactly one parent)\\n  projectId?: string;\\n  // Status update UUID (provide exactly one parent). Resolve status updates via `get_status_updates` first.\\n  statusUpdateId?: string;\\n  // Type of status update named by `statusUpdateId`, as returned by `get_status_updates`. Only valid together with `statusUpdateId`; omit to check both project and initiative status updates.\\n  statusUpdateType?: \\\"project\\\" | \\\"initiative\\\";\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"183d20\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007167,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":17,\"output\":\"\\n RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/apps/web\\n\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","create_time":1791339945.269017}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
