{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T02:27:31.869Z","ordinal":59450,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-69edda10-ff09-49d1-a78a-c5d2a6f90106","process_id":"66259","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","git diff -- docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json; git status --short; rg -n 'format:check:task|\"format\"|oxfmt' package.json; sed -n '296,317p' docs/architecture/frontend.md; rg -n 'values and execution|root registry|snapshot' docs/architecture/frontend.md apps/web/README.md | head -12"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git diff -- docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json; git status --short; rg -n 'format:check:task|\"format\"|oxfmt' package.json; sed -n '296,317p' docs/architecture/frontend.md; rg -n 'values and execution|root registry|snapshot' docs/architecture/frontend.md apps/web/README.md | head -12"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"diff --git a/docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json b/docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json\nindex 5ff858fc..e90ed738 100644\n--- a/docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json\n+++ b/docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n {\n   \"$schema\": \"https://taxkit.local/schemas/product-spec-task-plan.v1.json\",\n   \"spec\": \"docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md\",\n-  \"title\": \"Clean slate TaxKit foundation — implementation slices\",\n+  \"title\": \"Clean slate TaxKit foundation \\u2014 implementation slices\",\n   \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n   \"last_reviewed\": \"2026-10-07\",\n   \"authority\": \"Cooper explicitly authorised implementation, reviewable commits and draft PRs on 2026-10-04. No merge, deploy or publication; provider-plan approval remains separate.\",\n@@ -621,7 +621,8 @@\n       \"browserVerification\": [\n         \"Exercise browser tools with the supported experimental browser/agent when available, including visible form changes and results.\",\n         \"Verify fallback in an unsupported browser, cleanup after navigation, cancellation and equivalent results to manual UI/API.\",\n-        \"Run a real MCP client for each advertised adapter: current-version per-request metadata/list/read/call; older-version initialise/session/list/read/call. Prove version/header agreement, unsupported versions, origins/rates, real Worker session routing/expiry, streaming cancellation and cleanup; persist no tax figures in session metadata.\"\n+        \"Run a real MCP client for each advertised adapter: current-version per-request metadata/list/read/call; older-version initialise/session/list/read/call. Prove version/header agreement, unsupported versions, origins/rates, real Worker session routing/expiry, streaming cancellation and cleanup; persist no tax figures in session metadata.\",\n+        \"Restore checked server form/report/error through a paused first React render and completed hydration with a separate client registry; preserve retained answers and guidance without replay, then prove the next explicit request uses the restored form.\"\n       ],\n       \"qualityAudits\": [\n         \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n M apps/web/README.md\n M apps/web/package.json\n M apps/web/src/lib/calculator-page.container.tsx\n M apps/web/src/lib/calculator.atoms.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/calculator.boundary.browser.test.tsx\n M apps/web/src/lib/schemas.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/take-home.container.tsx\n M apps/web/src/routes/__root.tsx\n M apps/web/src/routes/calculators.$calculatorId.tsx\n M apps/web/test/native-pair.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/test/native-rpc-failures.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/vitest.native.config.ts\n M bun.lock\n M docs/architecture/frontend.md\n M docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md\n M docs/documentation-audit/README.md\n M docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md\n M docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json\n M docs/standards/tooling.md\n M docs/verification/critical-journeys.json\n M oxlint.config.ts\n M tools/oxlint/portable-rules.test.ts\n?? apps/web/src/lib/browser-tools.atoms.ts\n?? apps/web/src/lib/browser-tools.boundary.test.ts\n?? apps/web/src/lib/browser-tools.boundary.ts\n?? apps/web/src/lib/browser-tools.schemas.ts\n?? apps/web/src/lib/browser-tools.toolkit.ts\n?? apps/web/test/native-browser-tools.boundary.test.ts\n?? docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-browser-calculator-tools.json\n93:    \"format\": \"oxfmt -c oxfmt.config.ts --write . --no-error-on-unmatched-pattern\",\n94:    \"format:check\": \"turbo run //#format:check:task\",\n95:    \"format:check:task\": \"oxfmt -c oxfmt.config.ts --check . --no-error-on-unmatched-pattern\",\n153:    \"oxfmt\": \"0.71.0\",\ncleanup before asserting the restored guidance and next explicit request.\nThe Website also has a keyboard skip link, one main landmark, current-page\nnavigation, spaced controls and visible keyboard focus.\n\n\n## Page-owned browser tools\n\n`WebsiteBrowserToolkit` describes the five visible calculator commands separately\nfrom the remote tools. Its arguments reuse the owning form Schema, its catalogue\nuses the API contract, and its results reuse `WebsiteCalculatorViewState`.\nThat state also supplies the containers' readonly form/report/error presentation.\nRoutes restore server outcomes; no route selects an independent client answer.\n\nThe browser family holds one checked calculator description and uses the existing\n`calculatorRuntime.fn` registration command. Containers explicitly start it and\nsend `Atom.Interrupt` on cleanup. Relying on deferred registry garbage collection\nfor registration cleanup allowed the next page to collide with old tool names.\nThe registration scope's `FiberSet.makeRuntimePromise` is the single callback\nbridge; it creates no independent ManagedRuntime or backend client. Each native\nmethod retains its original receiver and its own abortable two-second limit.\n\nOne checked request object identifies each visible attempt. The handler waits for\napps/web/README.md:224:The root registry seeds settings and the catalogue; a later form restoration must not depend\napps/web/README.md:233:The registry still owns values and execution.\napps/web/README.md:505:marked out of date after editing or interruption. The shared page snapshot stays\napps/web/README.md:506:in memory until the root registry is disposed. This keeps once-restored server\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:267:values and execution. The shared page view uses `Atom.keepAlive` for the root\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:272:in-memory snapshots and the scoped client. No browser storage is added.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json b/docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json\nindex 5ff858fc..e90ed738 100644\n--- a/docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json\n+++ b/docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n {\n   \"$schema\": \"https://taxkit.local/schemas/product-spec-task-plan.v1.json\",\n   \"spec\": \"docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md\",\n-  \"title\": \"Clean slate TaxKit foundation — implementation slices\",\n+  \"title\": \"Clean slate TaxKit foundation \\u2014 implementation slices\",\n   \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n   \"last_reviewed\": \"2026-10-07\",\n   \"authority\": \"Cooper explicitly authorised implementation, reviewable commits and draft PRs on 2026-10-04. No merge, deploy or publication; provider-plan approval remains separate.\",\n@@ -621,7 +621,8 @@\n       \"browserVerification\": [\n         \"Exercise browser tools with the supported experimental browser/agent when available, including visible form changes and results.\",\n         \"Verify fallback in an unsupported browser, cleanup after navigation, cancellation and equivalent results to manual UI/API.\",\n-        \"Run a real MCP client for each advertised adapter: current-version per-request metadata/list/read/call; older-version initialise/session/list/read/call. Prove version/header agreement, unsupported versions, origins/rates, real Worker session routing/expiry, streaming cancellation and cleanup; persist no tax figures in session metadata.\"\n+        \"Run a real MCP client for each advertised adapter: current-version per-request metadata/list/read/call; older-version initialise/session/list/read/call. Prove version/header agreement, unsupported versions, origins/rates, real Worker session routing/expiry, streaming cancellation and cleanup; persist no tax figures in session metadata.\",\n+        \"Restore checked server form/report/error through a paused first React render and completed hydration with a separate client registry; preserve retained answers and guidance without replay, then prove the next explicit request uses the restored form.\"\n       ],\n       \"qualityAudits\": [\n         \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n M apps/web/README.md\n M apps/web/package.json\n M apps/web/src/lib/calculator-page.container.tsx\n M apps/web/src/lib/calculator.atoms.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/calculator.boundary.browser.test.tsx\n M apps/web/src/lib/schemas.ts\n M apps/web/src/lib/take-home.container.tsx\n M apps/web/src/routes/__root.tsx\n M apps/web/src/routes/calculators.$calculatorId.tsx\n M apps/web/test/native-pair.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/test/native-rpc-failures.boundary.test.ts\n M apps/web/vitest.native.config.ts\n M bun.lock\n M docs/architecture/frontend.md\n M docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md\n M docs/documentation-audit/README.md\n M docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md\n M docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json\n M docs/standards/tooling.md\n M docs/verification/critical-journeys.json\n M oxlint.config.ts\n M tools/oxlint/portable-rules.test.ts\n?? apps/web/src/lib/browser-tools.atoms.ts\n?? apps/web/src/lib/browser-tools.boundary.test.ts\n?? apps/web/src/lib/browser-tools.boundary.ts\n?? apps/web/src/lib/browser-tools.schemas.ts\n?? apps/web/src/lib/browser-tools.toolkit.ts\n?? apps/web/test/native-browser-tools.boundary.test.ts\n?? docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-browser-calculator-tools.json\n93:    \"format\": \"oxfmt -c oxfmt.config.ts --write . --no-error-on-unmatched-pattern\",\n94:    \"format:check\": \"turbo run //#format:check:task\",\n95:    \"format:check:task\": \"oxfmt -c oxfmt.config.ts --check . --no-error-on-unmatched-pattern\",\n153:    \"oxfmt\": \"0.71.0\",\ncleanup before asserting the restored guidance and next explicit request.\nThe Website also has a keyboard skip link, one main landmark, current-page\nnavigation, spaced controls and visible keyboard focus.\n\n\n## Page-owned browser tools\n\n`WebsiteBrowserToolkit` describes the five visible calculator commands separately\nfrom the remote tools. Its arguments reuse the owning form Schema, its catalogue\nuses the API contract, and its results reuse `WebsiteCalculatorViewState`.\nThat state also supplies the containers' readonly form/report/error presentation.\nRoutes restore server outcomes; no route selects an independent client answer.\n\nThe browser family holds one checked calculator description and uses the existing\n`calculatorRuntime.fn` registration command. Containers explicitly start it and\nsend `Atom.Interrupt` on cleanup. Relying on deferred registry garbage collection\nfor registration cleanup allowed the next page to collide with old tool names.\nThe registration scope's `FiberSet.makeRuntimePromise` is the single call