{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T02:47:31.499Z","ordinal":59772,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a11442-4bab-7503-a9b5-702c8d29e736","call_id":"call_FyB4dsDKar8YFqQffD9d5xyS","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"8690ab\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2914,\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"web\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\",\\n  \\\"imports\\\": {\\n    \\\"#/*\\\": \\\"./src/*\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"dev\\\": \\\"portless run --name taxkit vite dev\\\",\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"vite build\\\",\\n    \\\"check-types\\\": \\\"tsc --noEmit\\\",\\n    \\\"clean\\\": \\\"rm -rf .tanstack .turbo .wrangler dist node_modules/.vite\\\",\\n    \\\"test:browser\\\": \\\"vitest run --config vitest.browser.config.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"test\\\": \\\"bun --bun vitest run\\\",\\n    \\\"generate:worker-types\\\": \\\"wrangler types src/worker-runtime.generated.d.ts --include-env true --include-runtime true --strict-vars false --config wrangler.jsonc\\\",\\n    \\\"check:worker-types\\\": \\\"wrangler types src/worker-runtime.generated.d.ts --include-env true --include-runtime true --strict-vars false --config wrangler.jsonc --check\\\",\\n    \\\"build:native-pair\\\": \\\"cd ../.. && turbo run build --filter=api && bun --conditions=source run apps/web/scripts/native-pair-build.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"test:native-pair\\\": \\\"node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run --config vitest.native.config.ts\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"dependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"@effect/atom-react\\\": \\\"4.0.0\\\",\\n    \\\"@tanstack/react-router\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"@tanstack/react-start\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/api-http\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/api-rpc\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/content\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/core\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/docs-content\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/docs-fumadocs\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/rules-au-income-tax\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/rules-au-pay\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"alchemy\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"effect\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"react\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"react-dom\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"devDependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"@cloudflare/vite-plugin\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"@effect/platform-bun\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"@effect/platform-node\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"@effect/vitest\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"@modelcontextprotocol/client\\\": \\\"2.3.1\\\",\\n    \\\"@takumi-rs/wasm\\\": \\\"2.14.0\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/calculators\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"@types/node\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"@types/react\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"@types/react-dom\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"@vitejs/plugin-react\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"@vitest/browser-playwright\\\": \\\"5.0.3\\\",\\n    \\\"api\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"fumadocs-mdx\\\": \\\"15.4.6\\\",\\n    \\\"miniflare\\\": \\\"5.20261001.0-alpha\\\",\\n    \\\"playwright\\\": \\\"1.63.0\\\",\\n    \\\"scheduler\\\": \\\"0.28.0\\\",\\n    \\\"typescript\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"vite\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"vitest\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"webmcp-types\\\": \\\"0.1.10\\\",\\n    \\\"wrangler\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\nA remembered failure or interruption in AsyncResult is not the outcome of a\\nnew request while `waiting` is true. The policy container therefore hides old\\nrequest errors during waiting and displays the finished new failure only.\\nForm validation errors still appear immediately without sending a request.\\n\\n\\nThe root Website bootstrap also restores the checked API catalogue. Navigation\\nuses its titles, identities and context rather than a parallel local list.\\nThe additional calculator route restores only its own checked server report;\\nthe shared page state owns later browser reports and form/work/error policy. Each\\ncalculator's description group is retained by React while mounted because\\n`Atom.family` uses weak references. The registry owns the group's transient\\nvalues and execution. The shared page view uses `Atom.keepAlive` for the root\\nregistry's lifetime. This retains its checked form/outcome parents when a first\\nReact render pauses before subscriptions attach. Once-only initial-value hooks\\ncannot restore values that registry cleanup has already removed. Page cleanup\\nstill interrupts calculations and browser callbacks; root disposal releases\\nin-memory snapshots and the scoped client. No browser storage is added.\\nSaved submission admission checks calculator identity,\\nform shape and successful report shape together. No personal figure reaches\\nnavigation, page metadata, browser storage or a query string.\\n\\nThe standard HTML submission routes select their canonical calculator by the\\nclosed page address. Both extra pages display report-owned ledger explanation\\nand sources. The annual page explains the unresolved retained Medicare limit.\\nThe developer link and `/agents` route lead to actual API documentation,\\nOpenAPI and calculator metadata; they do not imply finished remote MCP or\\ncontent discovery.\\n\\n\\nThe registry provider seeds checked public settings and the catalogue. Each\\nfeature container uses `useAtomInitialValues` for its checked saved form on\\nthe owning page form atom before reading form state. Seeding a narrowed writable\\nprojection directly can leave its underlying form at the default amount.\\nThe route still owns transport restoration and result selection; this hook\\nadds no decoder or transport. Provider options apply only on its first render,\\nso saved form restoration must not depend on re-supplying those options.\\nThe native fixture uses different saved figures from initial examples and\\nchecks server HTML, hydrated fields, retained reports and no replay. A focused\\nbrowser fixture uses separate server/client registries, deliberately exercises\\nan unobserved first render and cleanup, then waits for client mounting and idle\\ncleanup before asserting the restored guidance and next explicit request.\\napps/web/README.md:231:uses weak references; holding only one member does not retain its grouping\\napps/web/README.md:497:## Visible calculator browser tools\\napps/web/README.md:505:marked out of date after editing or interruption. The shared page snapshot stays\\napps/web/README.md:507:answers and errors through a paused first React render and later navigation.\\ndocs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json:434:        \\\"Update package examples, generated snapshots, export/consumer fixtures, supported-scope public copy and Changesets with the new interface.\\\",\\ndocs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json:622:        \\\"Exercise browser tools with the supported experimental browser/agent when available, including visible form changes and results.\\\",\\ndocs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json:625:        \\\"Restore checked server form/report/error through a paused first React render and completed hydration with a separate client registry; preserve retained answers and guidance without replay, then prove the next explicit request uses the restored form.\\\"\\ndocs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json:640:        \\\"Remote and browser tools have actual caller evidence; lack of a supported browser is recorded as a proof gap, never a passed agent journey.\\\",\\ndocs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md:13:tests, graph validation, trace snapshots, API/SDK parity and build/type health.\\ndocs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md:27:- trace snapshots\\ndocs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md:174:local release journeys or historical HGI/HFI snapshots. 