{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T02:48:46.093Z","ordinal":59825,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0d067e63-d1a8-428b-8f8f-2b86173ef79a","process_id":"15661","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '158,224p' docs/verification/critical-journeys.json && sed -n '595,625p' docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-browser-calculator-tools.json && cat /private/tmp/dev77-browser-pr-body-draft.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '158,224p' docs/verification/critical-journeys.json","name":"critical-journeys.json","path":"docs/verification/critical-journeys.json"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '595,625p' docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-browser-calculator-tools.json","name":"2026-10-07-browser-calculator-tools.json","path":"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-browser-calculator-tools.json"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /private/tmp/dev77-browser-pr-body-draft.md","name":"dev77-browser-pr-body-draft.md","path":"/private/tmp/dev77-browser-pr-body-draft.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"      \"id\": \"taxkit-native-website\",\n      \"actorOrConsumer\": \"Calculator Website visitor, documentation reader and remote tool client\",\n      \"boundary\": \"Built and live native Website/private API binding/direct browser RPC and modern remote MCP and page-owned visible browser tools\",\n      \"startingState\": \"Selected Node and Chromium and the isolated local fixture ports are available; the MCP network client uses a dynamically allocated loopback TCP port.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        \"Native Alchemy source-built API and Website\",\n        \"Retained take-home example: 1654 dollars weekly, threshold claimed\",\n        \"Retained withholding example: 9500 dollars monthly, threshold not claimed\",\n        \"Retained annual example: 67000 dollars taxable income\",\n        \"Accepted 61-page documentation catalogue and matching compiled MDX presentation\",\n        \"Official MCP client 2.3.1 against the built native API over local TCP\",\n        \"Chrome153 native WebMCP caller with experimental feature enabled in a disposable context\"\n      ],\n      \"stepsOrProcedureOwner\": \"bun run web:test:native-pair\",\n      \"expectedBehavior\": [\n        \"Initial rendering makes no calculation; explicit Calculate produces 1301 dollars take-home pay through the private binding and direct browser POST /rpc.\",\n        \"Idle settings remain available; repeated Worker calls finish; editing cancels unfinished work and keeps the previous successful answer visibly out of date until a successful explicit calculation; the form also works without JavaScript.\",\n        \"Checked errors restore safely in the browser; native request limits and production import boundaries hold.\",\n        \"Data-free native settings GET succeeds; unexpected query/method input is rejected before framework parsing; an actual internal settings defect returns empty 500 and fixed safe logs.\",\n        \"Unknown, extended or missing native settings function addresses return empty 404 before framework lookup/logging; native generated URL owns identity.\",\n        \"Controlled slow headers and an unfinished actual reply reach the ten-second deadline; browser requests abort after the deadline, editing and browser Back leaving the form.\",\n        \"Real native CLI local development supplies both addresses/bindings, reloads API and Website source, restores exact sources and closes app ports on scoped shutdown.\",\n        \"Both actual saved local resources have explicitly disabled platform log/trace collection and zero sampling; source restoration uses the non-polling watcher and requires both visible page updates.\",\n        \"Take-home explanation opens with the keyboard without calculation; breakdown, recorded threshold and rule sources remain attached to the old report after form edits.\",\n        \"Catalogue-backed navigation offers all three calculators; withholding and annual pages start with their own empty result and return the retained 2756 and 12228 dollar answers through real browser RPC and standard HTML POST without JavaScript.\",\n        \"The new pages retain their own report and explanation after edits without another request; the annual Medicare limitation stays visible and the agent route links to actual API descriptions.\",\n        \"All supported native HTML form POST paths and public HTTP/RPC reject more than 64 KiB of encoded text with fixed safe HTML 413 form guidance or checked JSON 413 API guidance; public rejection preserves the Website CORS policy.\",\n        \"All nine closed named calculator RPC calls return checked canonical results; the seven additional metadata calls run through the real built API Worker.\",\n        \"Reached metadata work times out at five seconds through both actual HTTP and the generated RPC client; HTTP 504 keeps CORS and safe cleanup is observed. Metadata takes no calculation place.\",\n        \"All 61 accepted pages return real SSR articles with matching headings, navigation, title, description, canonical and checked Markdown link; missing public pages return native HTML 404.\",\n        \"Native data-free documentation GET accepts only bounded public page headers; original SSR addresses cannot be overridden by headers. Invalid query/content-type/page inputs reject before framework parsing.\",\n        \"Cold body/metadata/module mismatch and damaged native browser transport show safe recoverable guidance. Internal sidebar/authored links use native GET without document reload, with one current-page marker and deliberate heading focus; hydration preserves initial focus.\",\n        \"Mobile navigation and table scrolling work with the keyboard, horizontal content stays inside the article and ordinary documentation links work without JavaScript.\",\n        \"The accepted-catalogue search form retains literal URL words and Unicode, checks duplicate/unknown keys and bounded native URI headers, distinguishes empty/no-match/unavailable states and uses safe recoverable damaged-transport guidance.\",\n        \"Search native navigation retains the document; actual standard GET submission and result links work without JavaScript, with keyboard focus and contained phone layout.\",\n        \"After printed local addresses, served-page readiness retries only 502/503 for at most fifteen seconds; actual browser navigation still requires 200 and its expected heading.\",\n        \"Four conventional discovery files derive from the accepted catalogue and checked stage origins through the private API client; actual GET/HEAD headers and bodies, XML parsing, all canonical addresses and safe unavailable/method/query responses hold.\",\n        \"All accepted pages serve their exact processed body at the original address with checked Markdown preference and explicit .md links; GET/HEAD headers, Vary preservation, browser links and safe invalid/missing/unavailable replies hold without personal report downloads.\",\n        \"All accepted documentation pages have deterministic bounded 1200 by 630 PNG share assets, actual static GET/HEAD media/cache and matching HTML metadata/decoded TechArticle; Chromium decodes every served image and build-only renderer/WebAssembly stay out of Worker/browser outputs.\",\n        \"Modern MCP lists six canonical tools; its actual network client gets the same retained report and accepted Markdown page as HTTP. Alternating HTTP/MCP calculations exhaust one local allowance, with safe manual-retry failure and no submitted figures in captured logs.\",\n        \"Five mounted browser tools use the visible commands and shared state: no calculation on mount/read; actual fill/calculate/read equals a completed manual RPC; excess fields reject; editing keeps a stale answer; busy calls reject; caller/edit/page cancellation stops unfinished callbacks and manual retry still succeeds.\"\n      ],\n      \"expectedSideEffects\": [\n        \"Ignored native build files, scoped local Workers and Chromium only.\"\n      ],\n      \"preservedInvariants\": [\n        \"Retained tax results and existing docs operations stay unchanged.\",\n        \"No provider, state, credentials, deployment or publication operation.\"\n      ],\n      \"oracle\": \"Actual native built artifacts run in workerd; real Chromium independently confirms the exact RPC endpoint, no initial/replayed call, no trace/cookie headers and the retained answer. The API artifact contains the engine marker while browser artifacts must not. The generated native settings identity, short request marker and source-built internal defect require actual responses and positive fixed reporting; removing the owning failure boundary makes marker reflection fail the saved test. Unknown native function-address requests must return empty 404 and must omit the short request marker from actual native logs; removing exact-address admission restores that log leak. Actual built API global/procedure/fatal replies use fixed safe values; expected/version errors retain checked identity. A source-built damaged valid-JSON reply must restore a checked error through the genuine Website binding, with real Chromium editing and no replay. Positive fixed host logs omit the marker and pay values. Removal of each native encoder or the owned reply decoder must fail the saved test, followed by exact restoration and fresh dependency/artifact builds. Controlled API roots retain the real calculation/encoding and delay headers or the remaining body for twelve seconds. Actual generated clients must hit the ten-second deadline; Chromium must observe request abort after deadline, editing and actual Back route departure. Removing deadline or edit interruption fails the saved test; exact restoration and fresh builds pass. Pay-value checks inspect emitted log messages; private text checks inspect the whole record. Actual native mock-plan properties and saved real CLI state must contain the disabled collection policy; removing the API graph property fails the saved state Schema after runtime checks. These are declared-state checks, not cloud upload or exported-row proof. An actual successful browser answer survives edits, controlled unavailable retry and invalid form without being presented as current. Reverting figures makes no request and still needs one explicit real RPC to clear the stale message. Actual Worker-generated successful submission HTML hydrates without replay and retains its answer through editing and failed retry. The additional pages must independently return both known results via real API artifacts; no calculation fixture supplies them. Each page starts without the previous calculator's answer. Saved forms and report identity are checked together. Exact browser locator fill admissions have actual CLI positive and neighbouring-application negative fixtures. The size oracle uses multi-byte text below 65536 characters but above 65536 encoded bytes at both API paths and all three form paths. API boundary fixtures also accept exactly 65536 bytes and reject progressive streams without reading their tail. The bounded private client must classify an actual native 413 as the checked request-size error. Valid native calculator/catalogue replies at exactly 2 MiB succeed; over-limit streams stop before the tail and release. Status fixtures prove request-controller abort, safe serialized guidance and one call only. Six restored checked error variants hydrate with their guidance and no new calculation. The built shared-work fixture reaches eight calculations across one HTTP call and a seven-item RPC batch, refuses extra HTTP/SSR/public browser work, retains manual-retry guidance with no edit replay, emits checked HTTP 504/RPC timeouts at five seconds and reaches cleanup. The actual generated client preserves timeout identity. Direct scoped tests prove cancelled/failed place reuse and independent instance pools; timers do not claim forced CPU pre-emption. The owning native pair also reads detail/schema/graph/facts/rules/jurisdictions/tax years from the actual API artifact. The shared RPC corpus proves decoder, size, status, deadline, interruption and old-revision rejection for every named call. Documentation assertions inspect actual initial HTML for every page before independent Chromium navigation. Three source-built API variants retain valid checked pages but change Markdown, metadata or module identity; cold Website SSR and the actual native GET must detect each mismatch. A genuine server-function response is damaged in the browser to prove restoration rejects it. The API artifact must positively contain the executable calculator service identity and browser chunks must omit it; accepted documentation prose cannot stand in for an engine marker. Full-page images supplement functional observations only. Search SSR titles must match real built API results; the original URL resists a forged header. Native function identity is read from its compiled owner. A damaged genuine search reply must fail restoration. Actual form/result navigation and JavaScript-free submission are independently observed in Chromium. Focused browser navigation waits for rendered words before asserting checked outcomes; a bare router promise is insufficient. Bounded startup readiness cannot hide application errors or a persistent gateway failure. Actual built discovery GET bodies must equal the checked native client documents. Chromium XML parsing must produce the sitemap namespace and all 61 canonical addresses in catalogue order. Explicit HEAD 200 must have an empty body and GET-equivalent headers. A real unavailable API binding must return empty uncached 503. The actual RPC corpus rejects a valid document for a different requested path. The Markdown oracle compares all 61 same-page/file GET bodies and equal empty 200 HEAD headers with the owning processed catalogue. Real weighted/quoted/excluded/invalid Accept fields select actual HTML/text or empty safe errors; forged native page headers cannot change the original URL. Chromium independently parses alternate/visible links and opens the real file to exact processed text. Real unavailable binding and method/query/missing cases must fail safely. Share-asset proof reruns the actual build generator, compares every copied and served PNG byte, observes static GET/HEAD/cache/media and exactly accepted paths, decodes all 61 images in Chromium at 1200 by 630, and checks each actual head against the owning TechArticle Schema. Renderer/WebAssembly markers must be absent from Worker and browser outputs; encoded script text preserves unusual characters without closing the script. The actual official MCP network client runs against the source-built Worker, with native JSON/SSE parsing rather than handwritten frames. Its report/page decode through canonical Schemas and equal real HTTP replies; alternating transports exhaust the same local limiter. In-process real-client cancellation separately fills all eight places, cancels one, finishes a replacement and closes the others. This does not prove network cancellation or older session routing. Chrome153 actual native developer-tools events and invoke/cancel commands require real registration and native replies rather than a copied host object. A manual response witness must complete before answer equality. Pending real RPC is held at browser transport to prove busy admission, native caller abort, edit cancellation, successful manual retry and removal of five tools on route exit. Restored non-default pay fields, shared view and next checked request must agree. This is a test-controlled native caller, not an autonomous model session.\",\n      \"environment\": \"Local TaxKit checkout, native workerd and Chromium\",\n      \"authority\": \"none\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-website.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-website-failures.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-local-development.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-trace-containment.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-stale-calculator-answer.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-take-home-explanation.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculator-catalogue-rpc.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculator-pages.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-request-body-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-client-response-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculation-work-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-closed-rpc-operations.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-request-operation-protections.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-connection.json\",\n    \"notApplicable\": [\n      \"New Changeset: private app/type-only dependency only; no public package contract or export changes\",\n      \"New operational procedure: existing native-pair and release commands unchanged\",\n      \"Canonical skill assets and root instructions unchanged\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"qualification\": {\n    \"state\": \"Corrected source b complete frozen local nine-check graph pending\",\n    \"command\": [\n      \"bun\",\n      \"run\",\n      \"release:check\",\n      \"--\",\n      \"--ci\"\n    ],\n    \"mode\": \"Local report-only CI graph; no publication or provider authority\"\n  },\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Native protocol caller is controlled by Playwright; no autonomous model agent session\",\n    \"Experimental feature enabled only in disposable test browser; no general browser support claim\",\n    \"Older remote adapter sessions, actual remote network cancellation and public setup remain unfinished\",\n    \"No deployment, public availability, provider state, merge or publication proof\"\n  ],\n  \"rollback\": \"Restore this slice to base commit 4b349e0d1605687d0c5670af3edcd4ffdb82481e; local only, no provider rollback needed\",\n  \"remaining\": [\n    \"Complete current-source checks and primary review\",\n    \"Commit/push/read back reviewable draft stacked on #156\",\n    \"Finish older MCP sessions, real remote cancellation and qualified public setup before T006 acceptance\"\n  ],\n  \"failedAttempts\": [\n    {\nSupported experimental browsers can discover calculators, read or fill the visible form, calculate and read its answer through five page-owned tools. These use the same checked form, page state, edit/submit commands and RPC client as manual use. Missing browser support keeps normal browser and HTML forms working.\n\nThe shared page view retains restored server answers and errors while the first browser render pauses. The earlier implementation could clear those values before React started watching them. The direct test now recreates that cleanup and waits for completed hydration. Page departure still removes tools and interrupts unfinished work; the root registry releases in-memory state and its client. No figures are written to browser storage.\n\nValidation: pending complete corrected local nine-check graph. Focused browser checks (21 cases), all built-app checks (13 cases across nine files), lint, types, both unused-code checks and documentation/runbook checks pass. The dated browser receipt preserves the failed first full graph, the failing direct reproduction, correction, source identities and proof limits. Actual Chrome153 native tool calls cover manual-result equality, refusal, busy calls, abort, edit, retry and route cleanup; controlled host tests separately cover fallback, original receiver and bounded registration.\n\nStacked on draft #156. DEV-77 remains In Progress for older remote sessions, real remote cancellation and public setup. This is native caller testing controlled by the test, not an autonomous model session or public availability. Metrics remain deferred and retained tax results are unchanged. No merge, deployment, publication or provider apply is included. No Changeset: private Website plus a type-only dependency; no public package contract changes.\n\nRefs DEV-77.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"      \"id\": \"taxkit-native-website\",\n      \"actorOrConsumer\": \"Calculator Website visitor, documentation reader and remote tool client\",\n      \"boundary\": \"Built and live native Website/private API binding/direct browser RPC and modern remote MCP and page-owned visible browser tools\",\n      \"startingState\": \"Selected Node and Chromium and the isolated local fixture ports are available; the MCP network client uses a dynamically allocated loopback TCP port.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        \"Native Alchemy source-built API and Website\",\n        \"Retained take-home example: 1654 dollars weekly, threshold claimed\",\n        \"Retained withholding example: 9500 dollars monthly, threshold not claimed\",\n        \"Retained annual example: 67000 dollars taxable income\",\n        \"Accepted 61-page documentation catalogue and matching compiled MDX presentation\",\n        \"Official MCP client 2.3.1 against the built native API over local TCP\",\n        \"Chrome153 native WebMCP caller with experimental feature enabled in a disposable context\"\n      ],\n      \"stepsOrProcedureOwner\": \"bun run web:test:native-pair\",\n      \"expectedBehavior\": [\n        \"Initial rendering makes no calculation; explicit Calculate produces 1301 dollars take-home pay through the private binding and direct browser POST /rpc.\",\n        \"Idle settings remain available; repeated Worker calls finish; editing cancels unfinished work and keeps the previous successful answer visibly out of date until a successful explicit calculation; the form also works without JavaScript.\",\n        \"Checked errors restore safely in the browser; native request limits and production import boundaries hold.\",\n        \"Data-free native settings GET succeeds; unexpected query/method input is rejected before framework parsing; an actual internal settings defect returns empty 500 and fixed safe logs.\",\n        \"Unknown, extended or missing native settings function addresses return empty 404 before framework lookup/logging; native generated URL owns identity.\",\n        \"Controlled slow headers and an unfinished actual reply reach the ten-second deadline; browser requests abort after the deadline, editing and browser Back leaving the form.\",\n        \"Real native CLI local development supplies both addresses/bindings, reloads API and Website source, restores exact sources and closes app ports on scoped shutdown.\",\n        \"Both actual saved local resources have explicitly disabled platform log/trace collection and zero sampling; source restoration uses the non-polling watcher and requires both visible page updates.\",\n        \"Take-home explanation opens with the keyboard without calculation; breakdown, recorded threshold and rule sources remain attached to the old report after form edits.\",\n        \"Catalogue-backed navigation offers all three calculators; withholding and annual pages start with their own empty result and return the retained 2756 and 12228 dollar answers through real browser RPC and standard HTML POST without JavaScript.\",\n        \"The new pages retain their own report and explanation after edits without another request; the annual Medicare limitation stays visible and the agent route links to actual API descriptions.\",\n        \"All supported native HTML form POST paths and public HTTP/RPC reject more than 64 KiB of encoded text with fixed safe HTML 413 form guidance or checked JSON 413 API guidance; public rejection preserves the Website CORS policy.\",\n        \"All nine closed named calculator RPC calls return checked canonical results; the seven additional metadata calls run through the real built API Worker.\",\n        \"Reached metadata work times out at five seconds through both actual HTTP and the generated RPC client; HTTP 504 keeps CORS and safe cleanup is observed. Metadata takes no calculation place.\",\n        \"All 61 accepted pages return real SSR articles with matching headings, navigation, title, description, canonical and checked Markdown link; missing public pages return native HTML 404.\",\n        \"Native data-free documentation GET accepts only bounded public page headers; original SSR addresses cannot be overridden by headers. Invalid query/content-type/page inputs reject before framework parsing.\",\n        \"Cold body/metadata/module mismatch and damaged native browser transport show safe recoverable guidance. Internal sidebar/authored links use native GET without document reload, with one current-page marker and deliberate heading focus; hydration preserves initial focus.\",\n        \"Mobile navigation and table scrolling work with the keyboard, horizontal content stays inside the article and ordinary documentation links work without JavaScript.\",\n        \"The accepted-catalogue search form retains literal URL words and Unicode, checks duplicate/unknown keys and bounded native URI headers, distinguishes empty/no-match/unavailable states and uses safe recoverable damaged-transport guidance.\",\n        \"Search native navigation retains the document; actual standard GET submission and result links work without JavaScript, with keyboard focus and contained phone layout.\",\n        \"After printed local addresses, served-page readiness retries only 502/503 for at most fifteen seconds; actual browser navigation still requires 200 and its expected heading.\",\n        \"Four conventional discovery files derive from the accepted catalogue and checked stage origins through the private API client; actual GET/HEAD headers and bodies, XML parsing, all canonical addresses and safe unavailable/method/query responses hold.\",\n        \"All accepted pages serve their exact processed body at the original address with checked Markdown preference and explicit .md links; GET/HEAD headers, Vary preservation, browser links and safe invalid/missing/unavailable replies hold without personal report downloads.\",\n        \"All accepted documentation pages have deterministic bounded 1200 by 630 PNG share assets, actual static GET/HEAD media/cache and matching HTML metadata/decoded TechArticle; Chromium decodes every served image and build-only renderer/WebAssembly stay out of Worker/browser outputs.\",\n        \"Modern MCP lists six canonical tools; its actual network client gets the same retained report and accepted Markdown page as HTTP. Alternating HTTP/MCP calculations exhaust one local allowance, with safe manual-retry failure and no submitted figures in captured logs.\",\n        \"Five mounted browser tools use the visible commands and shared state: no calculation on mount/read; actual fill/calculate/read equals a completed manual RPC; excess fields reject; editing keeps a stale answer; busy calls reject; caller/edit/page cancellation stops unfinished callbacks and manual retry still succeeds.\"\n      ],\n      \"expectedSideEffects\": [\n        \"Ignored native build files, scoped local Workers and Chromium only.\"\n      ],\n      \"preservedInvariants\": [\n        \"Retained tax results and existing docs operations stay unchanged.\",\n        \"No provider, state, credentials, deployment or publication operation.\"\n      ],\n      \"oracle\": \"Actual native built artifacts run in workerd; real Chromium independently confirms the exact RPC endpoint, no initial/replayed call, no trace/cookie headers and the retained answer. The API artifact contains the engine marker while browser artifacts must not. The generated native settings identity, short request marker and source-built internal defect require actual responses and positive fixed reporting; removing the owning failure boundary makes marker reflection fail the saved test. Unknown native function-address requests must return empty 404 and must omit the short request marker from actual native logs; removing exact-address admission restores that log leak. Actual built API global/procedure/fatal replies use fixed safe values; expected/version errors retain checked identity. A source-built damaged valid-JSON reply must restore a checked error through the genuine Website binding, with real Chromium editing and no replay. Positive fixed host logs omit the marker and pay values. Removal of each native encoder or the owned reply decoder must fail the saved test, followed by exact restoration and fresh dependency/artifact builds. Controlled API roots retain the real calculation/encoding and delay headers or the remaining body for twelve seconds. Actual generated clients must hit the ten-second deadline; Chromium must observe request abort after deadline, editing and actual Back route departure. Removing deadline or edit interruption fails the saved test; exact restoration and fresh builds pass. Pay-value checks inspect emitted log messages; private text checks inspect the whole record. Actual native mock-plan properties and saved real CLI state must contain the disabled collection policy; removing the API graph property fails the saved state Schema after runtime checks. These are declared-state checks, not cloud upload or exported-row proof. An actual successful browser answer survives edits, controlled unavailable retry and invalid form without being presented as current. Reverting figures makes no request and still needs one explicit real RPC to clear the stale message. Actual Worker-generated successful submission HTML hydrates without replay and retains its answer through editing and failed retry. The additional pages must independently return both known results via real API artifacts; no calculation fixture supplies them. Each page starts without the previous calculator's answer. Saved forms and report identity are checked together. Exact browser locator fill admissions have actual CLI positive and neighbouring-application negative fixtures. The size oracle uses multi-byte text below 65536 characters but above 65536 encoded bytes at both API paths and all three form paths. API boundary fixtures also accept exactly 65536 bytes and reject progressive streams without reading their tail. The bounded private client must classify an actual native 413 as the checked request-size error. Valid native calculator/catalogue replies at exactly 2 MiB succeed; over-limit streams stop before the tail and release. Status fixtures prove request-controller abort, safe serialized guidance and one call only. Six restored checked error variants hydrate with their guidance and no new calculation. The built shared-work fixture reaches eight calculations across one HTTP call and a seven-item RPC batch, refuses extra HTTP/SSR/public browser work, retains manual-retry guidance with no edit replay, emits checked HTTP 504/RPC timeouts at five seconds and reaches cleanup. The actual generated client preserves timeout identity. Direct scoped tests prove cancelled/failed place reuse and independent instance pools; timers do not claim forced CPU pre-emption. The owning native pair also reads detail/schema/graph/facts/rules/jurisdictions/tax years from the actual API artifact. The shared RPC corpus proves decoder, size, status, deadline, interruption and old-revision rejection for every named call. Documentation assertions inspect actual initial HTML for every page before independent Chromium navigation. Three source-built API variants retain valid checked pages but change Markdown, metadata or module identity; cold Website SSR and the actual native GET must detect each mismatch. A genuine server-function response is damaged in the browser to prove restoration rejects it. The API artifact must positively contain the executable calculator service identity and browser chunks must omit it; accepted documentation prose cannot stand in for an engine marker. Full-page images supplement functional observations only. Search SSR titles must match real built API results; the original URL resists a forged header. Native function identity is read from its compiled owner. A damaged genuine search reply must fail restoration. Actual form/result navigation and JavaScript-free submission are independently observed in Chromium. Focused browser navigation waits for rendered words before asserting checked outcomes; a bare router promise is insufficient. Bounded startup readiness cannot hide application errors or a persistent gateway failure. Actual built discovery GET bodies must equal the checked native client documents. Chromium XML parsing must produce the sitemap namespace and all 61 canonical addresses in catalogue order. Explicit HEAD 200 must have an empty body and GET-equivalent headers. A real unavailable API binding must return empty uncached 503. The actual RPC corpus rejects a valid document for a different requested path. The Markdown oracle compares all 61 same-page/file GET bodies and equal empty 200 HEAD headers with the owning processed catalogue. Real weighted/quoted/excluded/invalid Accept fields select actual HTML/text or empty safe errors; forged native page headers cannot change the original URL. Chromium independently parses alternate/visible links and opens the real file to exact processed text. Real unavailable binding and method/query/missing cases must fail safely. Share-asset proof reruns the actual build generator, compares every copied and served PNG byte, observes static GET/HEAD/cache/media and exactly accepted paths, decodes all 61 images in Chromium at 1200 by 630, and checks each actual head against the owning TechArticle Schema. Renderer/WebAssembly markers must be absent from Worker and browser outputs; encoded script text preserves unusual characters without closing the script. The actual official MCP network client runs against the source-built Worker, with native JSON/SSE parsing rather than handwritten frames. Its report/page decode through canonical Schemas and equal real HTTP replies; alternating transports exhaust the same local limiter. In-process real-client cancellation separately fills all eight places, cancels one, finishes a replacement and closes the others. This does not prove network cancellation or older session routing. Chrome153 actual native developer-tools events and invoke/cancel commands require real registration and native replies rather than a copied host object. A manual response witness must complete before answer equality. Pending real RPC is held at browser transport to prove busy admission, native caller abort, edit cancellation, successful manual retry and removal of five tools on route exit. Restored non-default pay fields, shared view and next checked request must agree. This is a test-controlled native caller, not an autonomous model session.\",\n      \"environment\": \"Local TaxKit checkout, native workerd and Chromium\",\n      \"authority\": \"none\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-website.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-website-failures.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-local-development.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-trace-containment.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-stale-calculator-answer.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-take-home-explanation.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculator-catalogue-rpc.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculator-pages.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-request-body-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-client-response-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculation-work-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-closed-rpc-operations.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-request-operation-protections.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-connection.json\",\n    \"notApplicable\": [\n      \"New Changeset: private app/type-only dependency only; no public package contract or export changes\",\n      \"New operational procedure: existing native-pair and release commands unchanged\",\n      \"Canonical skill assets and root instructions unchanged\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"qualification\": {\n    \"state\": \"Corrected source b complete frozen local nine-check graph pending\",\n    \"command\": [\n      \"bun\",\n      \"run\",\n      \"release:check\",\n      \"--\",\n      \"--ci\"\n    ],\n    \"mode\": \"Local report-only CI graph; no publication or provider authority\"\n  },\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Native protocol caller is controlled by Playwright; no autonomous model agent session\",\n    \"Experimental feature enabled only in disposable test browser; no general browser support claim\",\n    \"Older remote adapter sessions, actual remote network cancellation and public setup remain unfinished\",\n    \"No deployment, public availability, provider state, merge or publication proof\"\n  ],\n  \"rollback\": \"Restore this slice to base commit 4b349e0d1605687d0c5670af3edcd4ffdb82481e; local only, no provider rollback needed\",\n  \"remaining\": [\n    \"Complete current-source checks and primary review\",\n    \"Commit/push/read back reviewable draft stacked on #156\",\n    \"Finish older MCP sessions, real remote cancellation and qualified public setup before T006 acceptance\"\n  ],\n  \"failedAttempts\": [\n    {\nSupported experimental browsers can discover calculators, read or fill the visible form, calculate and read its answer through five page-owned tools. These use the same checked form, page state, edit/submit commands and RPC client as manual use. Missing browser support keeps normal browser and HTML forms working.\n\nThe shared page view retains restored server answers and errors while the first browser render pauses. The earlier implementation could clear those values before React started watching them. The direct test now recreates that cleanup and waits for completed hydration. Page departure still removes tools and interrupts unfinished work; the root registry releases in-memory state and its client. No figures are written to browser storage.\n\nValidation: pending complete corrected local nine-check graph. Focused browser checks (21 cases), all built-app checks (13 cases across nine files), lint, types, both unused-code checks and documentation/runbook checks pass. The dated browser receipt preserves the failed first full graph, the failing direct reproduction, correction, source identities and proof limits. Actual Chrome153 native tool calls cover manual-result equality, refusal, busy calls, abort, edit, retry and route cleanup; controlled host tests separately cover fallback, original receiver and bounded registration.\n\nStacked on draft #156. DEV-77 remains In Progress for older remote sessions, real remote cancellation and public setup. This is native caller testing controlled by the test, not an autonomous model session or public availability. Metrics remain deferred and retained tax results are unchanged. No merge, deployment, publication or provider apply is included. No Changeset: private Website plus a type-only dependency; no public package contract changes.\n\nRefs DEV-77.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7041},"formatted_output":"      \"id\": \"taxkit-native-website\",\n      \"actorOrConsumer\": \"Calculator Website visitor, documentation reader and remote tool client\",\n      \"boundary\": \"Built and live native Website/private API binding/direct browser RPC and modern remote MCP and page-owned visible browser tools\",\n      \"startingState\": \"Selected Node and Chromium and the isolated local fixture ports are available; the MCP network client uses a dynamically allocated loopback TCP port.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        \"Native Alchemy source-built API and Website\",\n        \"Retained take-home example: 1654 dollars weekly, threshold claimed\",\n        \"Retained withholding example: 9500 dollars monthly, threshold not claimed\",\n        \"Retained annual example: 67000 dollars taxable income\",\n        \"Accepted 61-page documentation catalogue and matching compiled MDX presentation\",\n        \"Official MCP client 2.3.1 against the built native API over local TCP\",\n        \"Chrome153 native WebMCP caller with experimental feature enabled in a disposable context\"\n      ],\n      \"stepsOrProcedureOwner\": \"bun run web:test:native-pair\",\n      \"expectedBehavior\": [\n        \"Initial rendering makes no calculation; explicit Calculate produces 1301 dollars take-home pay through the private binding and direct browser POST /rpc.\",\n        \"Idle settings remain available; repeated Worker calls finish; editing cancels unfinished work and keeps the previous successful answer visibly out of date until a successful explicit calculation; the form also works without Ja