{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T02:49:53.431Z","ordinal":59868,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a06a1baf-6837-4bf3-bfde-a2c23ec6e983","process_id":"18235","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('docs/verification/critical-journeys.json');x=json.loads(p.read_text())\ndef visit(v):\n if isinstance(v,dict):\n  if v.get('id')=='taxkit-native-website':\n   v['expectedBehavior'].append('Leaving the annual calculator, forcing actual Chrome garbage collection and returning preserves visible fields and the shared retained stale report without another RPC request; the retained view also holds its weak-family description group.')\n   v['oracle']+=' Actual HeapProfiler collection between departure and return must preserve the distinct annual amount and earlier report without a new request; keeping only registry value nodes cannot satisfy this oracle.'\n  for z in v.values(): visit(z)\n elif isinstance(v,list):\n  for z in v: visit(z)\nvisit(x);p.write_text(json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\n')\np=Path('docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md')\np.write_text(p.read_text()+'''\\n\\n## 2026-10-07 — Page description identity after browser memory cleanup\n\nPrimary review found another lifetime defect before browser delivery. The root\nregistry retained the view and its values, but the weak family could still lose\nthe grouping object after leaving a page. Returning then created a new group\nwith default fields while the old registry values remained. Earlier focused\nchecks retained the description while mounted and did not force collection\nbetween visits. The second full graph was interrupted after seven successful\nordered stages; all twenty-eight frozen sources matched. That partial result\nis not complete qualification.\n\nThe actual native caller now leaves the annual calculator, forces Chrome garbage\ncollection and returns. Before the correction the form reset from 77000 to\n67000. The same check passes after the retained view reads through its immutable\ndescription group. Fields, shared form and retained stale report survive without\nanother RPC request. This uses the existing weak family and root registry;\nthere is no custom cache, persistent store or extra runtime. Page cleanup still\nremoves registrations and interrupts unfinished work, and root disposal releases\nthe in-memory values and scoped client.\n\nTypes, lint, all twenty-one focused browser checks, a fresh native build and the\nnative return-after-collection caller passed. The current journey, task checks,\nfrontend and Website owners record both value and description lifetimes.\nThe corrected source c still needs the complete frozen nine-check graph and\ntested commit/push/draft delivery. T006 remains in progress.\\n''')\nPY"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('docs/verification/critical-journeys.json');x=json.loads(p.read_text())\ndef visit(v):\n if isinstance(v,dict):\n  if v.get('id')=='taxkit-native-website':\n   v['expectedBehavior'].append('Leaving the annual calculator, forcing actual Chrome garbage collection and returning preserves visible fields and the shared retained stale report without another RPC request; the retained view also holds its weak-family description group.')\n   v['oracle']+=' Actual HeapProfiler collection between departure and return must preserve the distinct annual amount and earlier report without a new request; keeping only registry value nodes cannot satisfy this oracle.'\n  for z in v.values(): visit(z)\n elif isinstance(v,list):\n  for z in v: visit(z)\nvisit(x);p.write_text(json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\n')\np=Path('docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md')\np.write_text(p.read_text()+'''\\n\\n## 2026-10-07 — Page description identity after browser memory cleanup\n\nPrimary review found another lifetime defect before browser delivery. The root\nregistry retained the view and its values, but the weak family could still lose\nthe grouping object after leaving a page. Returning then created a new group\nwith default fields while the old registry values remained. Earlier focused\nchecks retained the description while mounted and did not force collection\nbetween visits. The second full graph was interrupted after seven successful\nordered stages; all twenty-eight frozen sources matched. That partial result\nis not complete qualification.\n\nThe actual native caller now leaves the annual calculator, forces Chrome garbage\ncollection and returns. Before the correction the form reset from 77000 to\n67000. The same check passes after the retained view reads through its immutable\ndescription group. Fields, shared form and retained stale report survive without\nanother RPC request. This uses the existing weak family and root registry;\nthere is no custom cache, persistent store or extra runtime. Page cleanup still\nremoves registrations and interrupts unfinished work, and root disposal releases\nthe in-memory values and scoped client.\n\nTypes, lint, all twenty-one focused browser checks, a fresh native build and the\nnative return-after-collection caller passed. The current journey, task checks,\nfrontend and Website owners record both value and description lifetimes.\nThe corrected source c still needs the complete frozen nine-check graph and\ntested commit/push/draft delivery. T006 remains in progress.\\n''')\nPY"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":6125},"formatted_output":""},"started_at_ms":1791341393431,"completed_at_ms":1791341393431}}
