(session === undefined) {\n1084:                      // Each HTTP POST has its own transport ID, but cancellation belongs to the session.\n1086:                        requests.get(key)?.prepared.binding === session\n1171:            const session = isHttp\n1179:              isHttp ? key.profile === session?.negotiatedProfile : key.clientId === clientId\n1231:          // HTTP UUID sessions are stored separately and outlive request-scoped client IDs.\n1299:                clientStates.get(clientId)?.sessionHeaders ?? Headers.empty,\n1368: * Unlike `layerStdio` and `layerHttp`, this layer does not install a concrete\n1373: * @see {@link layerHttp} for an HTTP-backed layer that registers with `HttpRouter` and installs JSON-RPC serialization\n1431: * @see {@link layerHttp} for the single-endpoint HTTP transport\n1493:              selectedProtocol = McpRuntime.selectStatefulProtocol(protocols, offered)\n1537: * `layerHttp` always implements the single-endpoint Streamable HTTP topology.\n1540: * HTTP+SSE transport, GET SSE, event resumption, session expiry, or client\n1541: * session termination.\n1550:export const layerHttp = (options: {\n"},"started_at_ms":1791341466809,"completed_at_ms":1791341466809}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T02:51:06.858Z","ordinal":59899,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a11445-94ea-7df0-9e65-5f0cd9b9141a","call_id":"call_V4thyp8ozhuw8QaLPSH58qUa","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"ec5510\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000006959,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2762,\"output\":\"$ bun run --filter=@taxkit/scripts release:check --ci\\n@taxkit/scripts release:check: RUN  [verification] bun run verification\\n# DEV-77 older-session research candidate only\\n\\nThe modern candidate source is frozen during release qualification. This note is\\nnot repository policy, implementation, task acceptance or provider authority.\\n\\nInstalled Effect 4.0.0 owns the v2025_11_25 adapter; its instance-local state Map\\nhas no public expiry/termination control. Do not import its private internals or\\nadvertise cross-Worker routing based on the private single-process SDK probe.\\n\\nChecked Alchemy reference beta.75 at\\n808ef694b2e742a2bb76cb301da371e71421fa57: packages/alchemy DurableObject and\\nRpcDurableObjectNamespace source/tests plus its cross-worker guidance.\\nInstalled beta.80 owns actual modular DurableObject.make, same-script namespace\\nbinding and per-method scopes. Reference examples contain local mutable state,\\nraw Promise/JSON and provider operations; none is admitted as TaxKit style or\\nauthority. Effect rc.112 HttpEffect source was checked for host abort guidance;\\ninstalled stable source owns compatibility.\\n\\nA possible bounded native design is one fixed-name object per stage, not one\\nobject per caller. It would own an in-memory native older-protocol host, bounded\\ninitialisation admission and a short hard lifetime. Expiry closes the whole\\nnative host, invalidates old conversation IDs and requires reinitialisation.\\nDo not save tax requests/results or use caller-controlled object names. Choose\\nand justify actual limits in active intent before implementing. Native stage\\nnamespace binding must prove isolation and routing locally.\\n\\nCalculation/content operations must still call the API's named services through\\nexisting checked native RPC, with the original checked rate key supplied as a\\nprivate capability separate from JSON. The object must not own another engine,\\nrate limiter, calculation pool or event owner. Verify same-script self binding\\nand avoid a resource dependency cycle before choosing this design.\\n\\nOwned stop signals cannot be assumed to cross native Worker bindings. Real\\nnetwork cancellation/cleanup, expiry, capacity, reconnect/manual-retry behaviour\\nand different callers need actual local Worker/official-client proof. The SDK\\n2.3.1 transport inspected here clears session identity explicitly in\\nterminateSession; server DELETE 405 is permitted. This alone proves neither\\nexpired-session behaviour nor a complete older-client journey.\\n\\nNo repository, provider or external service mutation was made for this research.\\n\\nFurther installed-source observation while the candidate stays frozen:\\nDurableObject.make captures its caller's services; the native bridge reconstructs\\nthe Worker graph once per isolate/export and supplies that captured Context to\\nthe object. This may allow a narrow older-session owner to capture the existing\\ncalculator/content services directly, without a self-binding or duplicated\\nservice implementation. Qualify the exact installed make form and local binding\\nbefore choosing this alternative. The pool remains scoped to the native host,\\nnot a promised global quota. Native request signal transport across the object\\ncall still needs actual proof; do not infer it from the Context source.\\n\\n\\n2026-10-07 follow-up, while browser candidate is frozen:\\n- Installed Alchemy beta.80 DurableObject.make and beta.75 reference both capture\\n  the caller services; DurableObjectBridge reconstructs them once per isolate.\\n  The typed native stub's fetch uses the SDK Fetcher adapter, while ordinary RPC\\n  methods return an Effect Promise envelope without a request AbortSignal.\\n- Official Cloudflare request/compatibility docs require explicit\\n  enable_request_signal for incoming disconnect notification, and list\\n  request_signal_passthrough for forwarding a native request's signal.\\n  Both have no default date stated. DO container guidance explicitly says RPC\\n  methods do not receive a request signal. A fetch-shaped private DO boundary\\n  is therefore the candidate to qualify before choosing private RPC for MCP.\\n- Native SDK Fetcher keeps modified headers when minting a private trust field,\\n  and passes its current Effect signal to the original receiver's fetch.\\n  That source is not proof of actual network/DO cancellation.\\n- Installed native stateful runtime keeps initialise metadata in an instance Map\\n  and provides no public remove/expiry. Do not reach its private Map. Closing a\\n  bounded native host scope remains the candidate whole-session expiry method.\\n- Source references checked: receiving DurableObject.ts:1341-1381,\\n  DurableObjectBridge.ts:47-211, Fetcher.ts; reference beta.75\\n  DurableObject.ts:1221-1257; reference Effect rc.112 HttpEffect.ts:232-273;\\n  receiving ai/internal/mcpStatefulRuntime.ts. No tracked source was changed.\\nPrimary sources read on 2026-10-07:\\nhttps://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/request/\\nhttps://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/compatibility-flags/\\nhttps://developers.cloudflare.com/containers/api/durable-object-container/\\nhttps://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/examples/readable-stream/\\n\\n\\nThe private direct-HTTP-to-Minfiflare platform probes started actual native DO\\nwork but did not observe its request signal stop within two seconds, both before\\nheaders and while returning a stream; no flags, enable_request_signal only and\\nboth enable/passthrough all reported started=1/stopped=0. They are not TaxKit\\nproof and no provider/app source was changed. Installed Miniflare5's mandatory\\nentry worker uses compatibility date 2025-03-17 and only nodejs_compat plus\\nservice_binding_extra_handlers, before forwarding Request via service.fetch.\\nIt lacks both signal settings even when the selected application has them.\\nThis is a source-supported candidate explanation, not yet proved causal.\\nRetain local probe identities:\\n/private/tmp/dev77-do-signal-probe-result.json\\n/private/tmp/dev77-do-signal-stream-probe-result.json\\n/private/tmp/dev77-do-signal-probe.mjs\\nAn actual direct workerd socket or explicit owned forwarding cancellation must\\nbe qualified before claiming native network/DO cleanup.\\n\\n\\nA subsequent active-stream probe bypassed Miniflare's entry gateway through its\\ninstalled unsafeGetDirectURL and disposable 127.0.0.1 socket, with a periodic\\nactual reply body. The same native DO started once in each case. No flags kept\\nstopped=0; enable_request_signal alone and enable plus passthrough both reached\\nstopped=1, with stream-cancel count 0. Thus the direct active stream qualifies\\nsignal cleanup for that native platform fixture. It does not qualify an SDK-\\ncomposed TaxKit MCP request before headers, buffered reply or whole remote\\nsession design. Negative pre-header and silent-stream results remain recorded.\\n/private/tmp/dev77-do-signal-active-stream-probe-result.json\\n/private/tmp/dev77-do-signal-active-stream-probe-error.log\\nThe private script currently represents the final active-stream probe. Retain\\nall result files as distinct observations; do not treat earlier output as proof\\nof the later source. Application cancellation must still be tested with the\\nactual official MCP client and exact native application artifacts.\\n\\n\\nThe direct held-before-response experiment also reported stopped=0 for all\\nthree flag selections within the bounded two-second observation. It must not\\nbe confused with the positive periodic streamed response. The exact application\\nreply policy (currently bounded/materialised before returning) may therefore\\nmatter for real network cancellation. Verify using the actual app before\\nchanging protocol or frame handling. Do not qualify pre-header cleanup from a\\npost-header active-stream result.\\n/private/tmp/dev77-do-signal-direct-held-probe-result.json\\nInstalled native McpServer.ts:1081-1091 ignores HTTP cancellation notifications\\nwhen no stateful binding is present. A modern stateless request cannot be assumed\\ncancelled by a separate notification. Stateful matching belongs to the exact\\nnative binding. The existing receiving module owns that rule; no copied routing\\nMap or private-runtime import is authorised.\\n\\n\\nA private native stateful adapter/DO experiment on 2026-10-07 used Effect\\n4.0.0, official MCP client 2.3.1, actual bundled workerd DO and a direct local\\nnetwork socket. Both clients negotiated 2025-11-25, received distinct native\\nsession headers, listed two fixed fixture tools and read fixed values. A held\\ncall started once; official client abort sent one observed cancellation\\nnotification, and the actual server operation interrupted once. The other\\nsession remained usable. Explicit native host disposal returned 204 and the\\nnext old-session request returned 404. No figures/provider operation occurred.\\n\\nThis is preparation only: both sessions route to one fixed DO, the tools are\\nfixtures, and expiry is explicit whole-host disposal. It does not prove TaxKit\\nservices, shared allowance, Alchemy SDK composition, per-session affinity,\\nautomatic TTL/alarm expiry, modern buffered-response cancellation or actual\\napplication acceptance. Do not copy its raw class/counter/runner implementation\\ninto governed application code. The first driver was stopped because it used\\nan old three-argument callTool signature; receiving SDK 2.3.1 takes\\ncallTool(params, options). The corrected exact driver and outputs are pinned in:\\n/private/tmp/dev77-native-stateful-do-preparation-c-identities.json\\n/private/tmp/dev77-native-stateful-do-preparation-c-result.json\\n/private/tmp/dev77-native-stateful-do-preparation-c-error.log\\n\\nFurther receiving qualifications: native MCP HTTP initialise hard-codes a\\nrandom session UUID, while its stateful runtime has no public per-session\\nremoval/expiry. A provider affinity owner must preserve that native binding\\nrather than copy its session Map or protocol frames. SDK DurableObject beta.80\\nimplements getByName, but newUniqueId/idFromString/get remain commented out in\\nthe returned implementation despite its broad interface. Qualify the implemented\\noperation rather than assuming every declared method exists. References:\\nreceiving ai/internal/mcpRuntime.ts:525-535; Workers/DurableObject.ts:1315-1327;\\nCloudflare/Fetcher.ts native fetch and Effect signal; official client index.d.mts\\npublic callTool/sessionId/protocolVersion contracts. No tracked source changed\\nwhile the corrected browser candidate graph was running.\\n\\n\\nThe next actual application design must also bound repeated initialise calls.\\nReceiving mcpRuntime.ts:302-323 admits an existing session header for initialise,\\nand the native handler mints another session UUID. A provider-owned single-\\nsession host cannot assume that native storage is automatically bounded or\\nremoved. Any proposed affinity/expiry wrapper must use the native parser and\\nSDK lifecycle, preserve header/version semantics and close old host scope on\\ninvalid re-initialisation or expiry. No wrapper design is accepted by this\\nsource-only observation; actual tools, caller isolation, shared API work/rate\\npolicy and cleanup still need native application proof.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"72f084\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007167,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1138,\"output\":\"ap