{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T02:54:29.550Z","ordinal":60020,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d223c809-9e3c-49a0-9003-23e88b313291","process_id":"45555","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","git show HEAD:docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json | sed -n '570,750p'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show HEAD:docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json | sed -n '570,750p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-content-acceptance.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-content-http.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-native-docs-connection.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-connection.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-search.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-discovery.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-markdown.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-images.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-checks.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-release-detail-output.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-docs-retirement-manifest.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-docs-retirement.json\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CSF-T006\",\n      \"title\": \"Add remote MCP and visible browser agent tools\",\n      \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-005\",\n        \"CSF-006\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T004\",\n        \"CSF-T005\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Tool names, schemas and descriptions reflect current catalogue/content and use the same calculation owner.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Add native Effect remote MCP for catalogue/docs discovery, checked calculator inputs, execution and results, reusing the same named operations and accepted Markdown.\",\n        \"Select and qualify native Effect v2026_07_28 stateless and v2025_11_25 stateful adapters before advertising them. Apply anonymous request limits, allowed origins, bounded request/stream lifetimes, cancellation, typed errors and safe tool descriptions; publish discovery and setup docs.\",\n        \"Register feature-detected page-owned WebMCP tools for find/read/fill/calculate/read-result. Reuse visible website commands and the checked RPC client; unregister/cancel on route change or unmount. Do not add direct SDK/backend calls or a duplicate calculation/event owner.\",\n        \"Document actual browser support and distinguish protocol/schema registration from a real agent journey; ordinary browser use must keep working.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"apps/api native MCP adapter and justified contract exports at the existing package owners\",\n        \"apps/web page-owned WebMCP registration/command owner and cleanup tests\",\n        \"Public agent setup/Markdown docs, app/package READMEs, owning architecture and critical-journey updates\",\n        \"HTTP/MCP/WebMCP equality, origin/rate/cancellation and browser evidence\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run test\",\n        \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n        \"bun run check-types\",\n        \"bun run build\",\n        \"bun run check:docs\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Exercise browser tools with the supported experimental browser/agent when available, including visible form changes and results.\",\n        \"Verify fallback in an unsupported browser, cleanup after navigation, cancellation and equivalent results to manual UI/API.\",\n        \"Run a real MCP client for each advertised adapter: current-version per-request metadata/list/read/call; older-version initialise/session/list/read/call. Prove version/header agreement, unsupported versions, origins/rates, real Worker session routing/expiry, streaming cancellation and cleanup; persist no tax figures in session metadata.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"Tool names, schemas and descriptions reflect current catalogue/content and use the same calculation owner.\",\n        \"Remote and browser tools have actual caller evidence; lack of a supported browser is recorded as a proof gap, never a passed agent journey.\",\n        \"Anonymous access has bounded work and no required account or stored calculation.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CSF-T007\",\n      \"title\": \"Prepare DNS, domain and secret provider plans\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-007\",\n        \"CSF-010\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T003\",\n        \"CSF-T005\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"The reviewed plan names exact resources/account/stage and never creates or edits Production DNS for a Preview.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Read actual taxkit.dev zone/account, records, domain/registrar and DNSSEC state; classify existing state and preserve unrelated mail/verification records.\",\n        \"Declare adopted retained Production zone/settings and native taxkit.dev Website plus www redirect and api.taxkit.dev backend domain attachments; keep Preview away from Production DNS. Derive each host's own origin from native Cloudflare.Worker.URL and cross-host addresses from native resource Outputs, with application-ingress Schema checks and checked failure for absent Outputs. Qualify local, Preview and custom-domain behaviour; domains are infrastructure inputs, not duplicated application-origin configuration.\",\n        \"Complete native Doppler stage selection, shell-source policy, named runtime bindings and distinct deploy/query/Turbo credentials; remove stale --env-file wrappers only with equivalent behaviour.\",\n        \"Produce version-matched no-apply plans and authority/rollback/readback procedures. Replace graph validators/workflow projection assumptions that admit only one DocsWebsite without adding a bespoke parallel deployment framework.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"packages/infrastructure native zone/domain/stage/secrets graph and root alchemy entries\",\n        \"tools/docs-deployment/** owning admission/secret/workflow replacements, relevant workflows and Turbo inputs\",\n        \"docs/runbooks/docs-deployment.md, recovery.md, operations/authority-model.md and tools/documentation/runbook-contract.json\",\n        \"Redacted exact-resource plans, retention and DNS/secret readback procedures\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run check:docs-deployment:types\",\n        \"bun run check:docs-deployment-tools:types\",\n        \"bun run check:docs-deployment\",\n        \"bun run test:docs-deployment\",\n        \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n        \"bun run check:repository-paths\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"The reviewed plan names exact resources/account/stage and never creates or edits Production DNS for a Preview.\",\n        \"Doppler precedence, runtime binding and separate credential purposes have checked proof without secret values in output.\",\n        \"All cloud mutations remain unexecuted until the concrete plan has the required named authority; DNS/TLS/registrar readback is separate from apply success.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CSF-T008\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement minimal PostHog traffic and calculator analytics\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-008\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T004\",\n        \"CSF-T005\",\n        \"CSF-T006\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Only the documented events and fields leave the app; no persistent browser identity or consent dialogue is introduced.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Manage retained TaxKit Production and shared Preview projects through a private Alchemy Resource/Provider and current Distilled PostHog, with checked organisation/region/ownership and safe management failures.\",\n        \"Implement explicit pageviews in a private React-owned browser service and one successful hosted-calculation event owner in the backend application; honour a checked browser opt-out without linking identities.\",\n        \"Use a synchronous final-enrichment allowlist, memory-only persistence, explicit DNT and disabled automatic/replay/person features. Local and ordinary Preview capture stay off; no consent dialog.\",\n        \"Implement the bounded same-origin event relay and native backend capture through owned Effect HTTP. Qualify actual current SDK transport/disposal and no duplicate events; retain best-effort delivery limits.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"apps/web analytics service/live adapter/consumer/relay and route event ownership\",\n        \"apps/api application successful-use capture and checked collection policy\",\n        \"packages/infrastructure PostHog provider/resources/bindings and qualified optional provider fixes\",\n        \"Analytics tests, app/infra READMEs, privacy/public copy and deployment/recovery runbook sections\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run test\",\n        \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n        \"bun run check-types\",\n        \"bun run build\",\n        \"bun run check:docs\",\n        \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n     